msgid "The vulnerability"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"CVE-2026-114938, aka \"Java4Shell\", is a memory corruption bug in the OpenJDK Base64 decoder.\n"
"The JVM uses a CPU-optimized implementation (an _intrinsic_) to decode Base64.\n"
"A crafted Base64 input makes it write past its buffer.\n"
"Researchers demonstrated memory disclosure and remote code execution."
msgstr ""

msgid "Exploitation requires *all* of the following:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An unpatched OpenJDK 17.0.6+, 21, 25 or 27 build (all vendors: Temurin, Red Hat, Corretto, Zulu, etc.).\n"
"IBM Semeru is not affected: it uses the OpenJ9 JVM, not HotSpot, and does not include the vulnerable intrinsic."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An **x86-64** CPU exposing **AVX-512 VBMI** (on Linux: `avx512f`, `avx512bw`, `avx512vbmi` and `bmi2` in `/proc/cpuinfo`).\n"
"ARM64 is not affected."
msgstr ""

msgid "Base64 intrinsics enabled (the default)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The application decodes attacker-controlled Base64 data.\n"
"Almost every HTTP application does decode Base64: Basic auth headers, JWTs, request payloads."
msgstr ""

msgid "Oracle rates it CVSS 3.1 8.1. No exploitation in the wild is known at the time of writing."
msgstr ""

msgid "References:"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://www.tenable.com/blog/java4shell-cve-2026-114938-frequently-asked-questions-about-openjdk-rce-vulnerability[Tenable FAQ]"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://www.keycloak.org/2026/11/java4shell-vulnerability-cve-2026-114938[Keycloak advisory]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Is Quarkus affected?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"No. The bug lives in the JDK, not in Quarkus.\n"
"Upgrading Quarkus does not fix it.\n"
"Fixing or mitigating the JDK does."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are deploying a Quarkus application (in JVM mode) in a container, you are affected if your base image contains a vulnerable JDK.\n"
"So, make sure you update your base image, and, if it's pointing to a floating tag, repull the image before rebuilding the container."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mitigation per deployment model"
msgstr ""

msgid "The workaround: <code>-XX:-UseBASE64Intrinsics</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `-XX:-UseBASE64Intrinsics` flag disables the vulnerable intrinsic.\n"
"The JVM falls back to the standard Java implementation of the `Base64` decoder, which is memory-safe.\n"
"The decoded output is the same.\n"
"Only the speed changes: decoding is slower, which rarely matters outside Base64-heavy workloads."
msgstr ""

msgid "You run your Quarkus application with a JDK installed on the host."
msgstr ""

msgid "If your JDK vendor shipped a fixed build and you installed it: you are fine."
msgstr ""

msgid "Otherwise: add `-XX:-UseBASE64Intrinsics` to the JVM options."
msgstr ""

msgid "Or, if you use `JAVA_OPTS` in your start scripts:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Remove the flag once a fixed JDK is deployed."
msgstr ""

msgid "This is the Quarkus recommended setup (`Dockerfile.jvm`, `registry.access.redhat.com/ubi9/openjdk-<version>-runtime` or `registry.access.redhat.com/ubi10/openjdk-<version>-runtime`)."
msgstr ""

